            for, not just lower than a reference price nobody pays. Horizon’s reference prices fail that test
            badly: the 7.0 AT’s $2,100 is almost double what it sells for, and none of the five treadmills sold
            at its reference price on any day we checked between October and late November 2026. So the
            comparison that matters is against the code and Amazon prices we recorded earlier.
