          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[560px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead><tr><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Price band</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Horizon (23 Nov)</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Sole (23 Nov)</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">The trade-off</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">About $800 to $900</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">T202, $799</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">F50, $899.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">The T202 has a 60-inch deck and 12 mph; the F50 has a 55-inch deck and 10 mph on its listing</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">About $950 to $1,100</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">7.0 AT, $934</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">F63, $1,099.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Both 20 x 60 in. and 12 mph; Horizon is about $165 less</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">About $1,500</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">7.4 AT, $1,499</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">F80, $1,499.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Horizon has the 22-inch deck; Sole a 10.1-inch touchscreen</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">About $1,800 to $2,000</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">7.8 AT, $1,799</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">F85, $1,999.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Both 22 x 60 in.; Sole gives the F85 a 15.6-inch touchscreen</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            Neither brand needs a subscription: Horizon’s treadmills connect over Bluetooth to third-party
            apps such as Zwift and the Peloton App, which you can use free or pay for as you choose, and Sole’s
            app is free. The difference is in the warranty, where Sole states a lifetime frame and motor
            warranty across its range and Horizon gives lifetime frame and motor cover with parts terms of one
            to five years by model. If you are choosing between brands rather than models, our <a href="/is-horizon-a-good-treadmill-brand/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">is Horizon a good treadmill brand</a> guide covers
            reliability and support, and the <a href="/nordictrack-black-friday-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">NordicTrack Black Friday deals</a> page covers the
            iFIT-based alternative.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="when-to-buy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>When to Buy: Before 27 November, or Wait?</h2>
<p>
            Horizon’s codes were live from 22 November and end at 11:59 pm Central on Friday 27 November.
            Cyber Monday is 30 November 2026. There are three reasonable approaches.
          </p>
          <ol>
            <li><strong>Buy the 7.8 AT this week if it is the one you want.</strong> $1,799 is $100 below
            anything we have recorded for it, and the code has a fixed end date.</li>
            <li><strong>Do not panic over the 7.0 AT, T202 or 7.4 AT.</strong> Their Black Friday prices
            match ones we saw in October or on 21 November, and Amazon was selling all three at the same
            money on 21 November, before the codes started. There is no evidence this week is the only chance
            to pay these prices, though there is no guarantee they come back either.</li>
            <li><strong>If you miss the deadline, check Amazon and Horizon again on Cyber Monday</strong>,
            and judge any price against the table on this page. Our <a href="/cyber-monday-treadmill-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Cyber Monday treadmill deals</a> page covers what usually
            changes between Friday and Monday.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>
            Stock matters too. The T101 Connect was already sold out on Horizon’s store, and on 13 October
            Horizon showed the 7.8 AT shipping the week of 26 October, so ship dates can stretch at busy
            times. Check the ship date on Horizon’s product page before you pay if you need the treadmill by a
            particular day. If you are not in a hurry, our guide to the <a href="/best-time-of-year-to-buy-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best time of year to buy a treadmill</a> covers the
            other sale windows.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="checklist" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Before You Click Buy: A Horizon Checklist</h2>
<ul>
            <li><strong>Check the circuit.</strong> Horizon asks for a dedicated 15 to 20 amp circuit with no
            GFCI outlet, surge protector or extension cord. If the room you have in mind does not have one,
            price an electrician into the deal. Our <a href="/horizon-treadmill-troubleshooting/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Horizon troubleshooting</a> guide explains why.</li>
            <li><strong>Measure the space.</strong> The T202’s Amazon listing gives assembled dimensions of
            76 by 34 by 57 inches and the 7.4 AT’s 76 by 37 by 63 inches. Allow clear space behind the deck as
            well.</li>
            <li><strong>Confirm the model.</strong> The 7.0 AT, 7.4 AT and 7.8 AT look alike in photos.
            Check the deck width (20 or 22 inches) and weight rating on the model in your basket.</li>
            <li><strong>Check the code applied.</strong> The basket should show the Black Friday price, not
            the everyday price, before you pay.</li>
            <li><strong>Price delivery and assembly.</strong> Compare the delivered total from Horizon and
            from Amazon, not the sticker price; a $1 gap on the sticker means nothing if delivery differs by
            $100.</li>
            <li><strong>Screenshot the price and date.</strong> If something goes wrong with the order, a
            dated record of the offer is the quickest way to sort it out.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            No subscription is needed on any Horizon treadmill, which keeps the five-year cost close to the
            purchase price. Our <a href="/best-treadmills-without-subscriptions/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmills without subscriptions</a> guide explains why that matters when comparing Horizon with brands built around paid classes.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Common mistakes -->
        <div id="common-mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Buying a Horizon at Black Friday? Avoid These 4 Mistakes</h2>
          <p>Horizon’s sale is straightforward once you ignore the reference prices. These four still catch buyers out.</p>
          <ol class="ed-mistakes not-prose">
            <li>
              <h3>Measuring the deal against the reference price</h3>
              <p>Horizon’s reference prices run from $999 to $2,699 and it does not sell at them. A “56% off” reading on the 7.0 AT tells you nothing. Compare the code price with what the model has actually sold for, using the table on this page.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Forgetting to enter the code</h3>
              <p>Horizon’s everyday prices are $100 to $300 above its Black Friday prices, and the saving only applies with the model’s code. Check the basket shows $799, $934, $1,499 or $1,799 before you pay.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Assuming delivery is free</h3>
              <p>Horizon’s Black Friday free shipping is advertised for bikes, not treadmills. Price standard, room-of-choice and assembly options at checkout, and compare the delivered total with Amazon’s.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Buying the T101 Connect because it is the cheapest name</h3>
              <p>It is sold out at Horizon, and Amazon’s $779.67 is only $20 below the T202’s Black Friday price. For that $20 the T202 gives a 60-inch deck, 12 mph and a 325 lb capacity.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <!-- The bottom line -->
        <div id="bottom-line" class="ed-bottomline">
          <h2>The bottom line</h2>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white">Horizon’s Black Friday codes are honest but mostly familiar.</strong> On
            23 November 2026 they put the T202 at $799, the 7.0 AT at $934, the 7.4 AT at $1,499 and the 7.8 AT
            at $1,799 on Horizon’s store until 27 November, with Amazon within a dollar on the first three. Only
            the 7.8 AT’s price is lower than anything we had recorded before; the others match earlier lows.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white">Buy the right model at these prices, not the biggest badge.</strong> For
            most buyers that is the 7.0 AT; for width and a higher weight rating, the 7.4 AT. Compare delivered
            prices, and see our <a href="/how-much-does-a-horizon-treadmill-cost/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">Horizon price guide</a> and <a href="/horizon-fitness/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">Horizon Fitness guide</a> for the range outside sale weeks.
          </p>
        </div>

